# Full-Width Awning and Plain Hero

Status: DONE
Milestone: M18 Storefront canopy correction
Dependencies: 22_COZY_WHOLE_SITE.todo

## Purpose

The owner wants the header canopy to cover the whole page width, inspired by
full-front shop awnings rather than a small floating ornament. The owner also
explicitly rejected the illustrated window behind the real hero cake.

## Tasks

- [x] Preserve the prior SVG, stylesheet, template, showcase and context bytes.
- [x] Remove page-awning side padding, maximum width and SVG letterboxing.
- [x] Draw deeper original striped fabric, projecting front bar and scalloped valance.
- [x] Retain the cream/blush colour family and padded entrance scene.
- [x] Remove the hero window from markup, styles, builder and public output.
- [x] Remove window-specific empty space above the real cake.
- [x] Check painted edge-to-edge coverage at320-2560px and100%/200%text.
- [x] Refresh the affected README images and public-safe overview.
- [x] Complete local/public regression checks and scoped publication with workstream24.

## Acceptance criteria

- Actual awning pixels, not just a wrapper, reach both viewport edges.
- No horizontal scrolling, clipped navigation or artwork over reading text.
- Original illustration only; no copied stock imagery, text or watermarks.
- Rejected hero window absent, with real cake/sticker bytes and label retained.
- Entrance glass/room/parallax/gesture bell/skip remain intact.
- No extra image-tool views or owner visual acceptance claimed.

